# The rclone-manager-tests commit this repository's gate runs its browser
# e2e suite and its CLI smoke slice from. Moved by
# scripts/e2e/bump-tests-pin.sh, and the commit that moves it is itself
# gated against the new pin, so a bad bump cannot land unnoticed.
#
# Why this repository pins that one, and that one pins a build of this one:
# pinning the tests repository means a new or changed test cannot break
# unrelated in-flight work here until someone bumps this line, and the bump
# is itself gated. Pinning the product build over there means a release
# cannot silently change what those suites certify. Each is one line, in one
# file, reviewable on its own.
#
# Deliberately held at 9dfd6e3 while rclone-manager-tests' main sits at 778891a.
#
# The next commit over there, 0f89776 ("Prove Suite B can see where a backup's
# copies are"), is eighteen browser cases written for #240, which puts an
# artifact's placements on screen. #240 has not landed here, so moving the pin
# past it turns 17 Suite B specs red against a product that was never supposed
# to satisfy them yet. I did exactly that once and the gate caught it, which is
# the pin doing its job rather than a problem with it.
#
# That is the arrangement working as designed: specs are allowed to land over
# there ahead of the feature, and this line is what stops them being enforced
# until the feature arrives. The bump belongs to #240's own pull request, which
# should move it to 778891a or later, NOT to 0f89776, so it picks up the
# equivalence matrix work from #376 at the same time.
#
# Nothing is lost by holding it. #376's fix is entirely in suites/equivalence,
# and this gate runs Suite A's smoke slice and Suite B, never Suite C.
TESTS_REPO_URL=https://github.com/spdrman/rclone-manager-tests.git
TESTS_REPO_SHA=57ef7b54169b17a3d21e3759c6b6e83d8c0e9c52
